  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The diagonal run – switch places and shoot first time",
  "description": "One goal with a goalkeeper. Line A stands just in front of their own goal crease and line B in the corner at the same goal. A runs without the ball diagonally out towards the boards and gets a forward pass from B. B sets off straight away on a diagonal run across the court into the slot, while A carries the ball along the boards. A passes in to B, who shoots first time, and A carries on towards goal for any rebound.\n\nPlayers switch lines after each turn. Run it just as much mirrored. Easier variant: two lines a little way from goal, one by each board, with a cone in front of line B. A rounds the cone, B plays a short pass to A and curves in towards the middle, A carries the ball a few steps and passes to B, who shoots first time. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "High tempo in every run – if you wait for the ball, you set off too late."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Pass flat and in front of your team-mate so they can take it in stride."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Shoot early and hard – do not carry the ball all the way to the goal line."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Whoever does not shoot always follows up for the rebound."
    }
  ],
